________________________________________1. Document Control & Overview
1.1 Project Title
Murex XVA (CVA & FVA) Pricing, Provisioning, and Risk Management Framework
1.2 Business Objective
The primary business objective is to implement a robust, enterprise-wide valuation adjustment framework within Murex (MX.3). The platform must support two core operational workflows:
1.	Real-Time Pre-Deal Incremental Pricing: Allow Front Office trading desks to calculate incremental counterparty credit and funding risk charges on new transactions or market operations prior to deal execution.
2.	End-of-Day Provisioning & Monitoring: Provide an immutable batch calculation engine for the PCVA desk, Finance (Product Control), and Risk Oversight to track daily XVA provisions, analyze risk sensitivities, calculate regulatory capital, and execute market hedges.
________________________________________2. Business Scope & Valuation Adjustments
2.1 In-Scope Valuation Adjustments
The system must calculate and report the following specific valuation adjustments:
●	Credit Valuation Adjustment (CVA): Measures counterparty credit risk by adjusting derivative transaction prices based on the potential loss if a counterparty defaults.
●	Funding Valuation Adjustment (FVA): Accounts for uncollateralized exposure funding costs and benefits, split strictly into:
○	Funding Cost Adjustment (FCA): Incurred when a positive Mark-to-Market (MTM) trade with an uncollateralized counterparty is hedged in the collateralized interbank market, requiring collateral to be funded.
○	Funding Benefit Adjustment (FBA): Incurred when a negative MTM with an uncollateralized counterparty yields collateral from the interbank market hedge without posting collateral back.
2.2 Out-of-Scope Valuation Adjustments
The following adjustments are explicitly excluded from calculation within the current platform scope:
●	Debit Valuation Adjustment (DVA)
●	Collateral Valuation Adjustment (ColVA)
●	Capital Valuation Adjustment (KVA)
●	Margin Valuation Adjustment (MVA)
