4.1 Eligibility Criteria Summary
●	Product Typology Scope:
○	Eligible: Interest Rate Swaps (IRS), FX Forwards, FX Options, and Commodity derivatives.
○	Ineligible: Short-settlement trades (FX Spot) and Fixed Income cash instruments (Bonds).
●	Portfolio & Counterparty Rules: Portfolios (including Wall Street feed source portfolios) and counterparties must be explicitly flagged with XVA Eligibility = True.
●	P&L Acceptance Filter (EOD vs. Live Engine):
○	EOD Viewer: Restricted exclusively to P&L Accepted deals.
○	Live Engine (RTLIM): Evaluates all active, existing deals in the system regardless of P&L acceptance state to capture full active market risk.
________________________________________5. Functional Requirements
5.1 Real-Time Live Engine (RTLIM) Workflow
●	Start-of-Day Baseline Build: The live engine (RTLIM) must generate every morning (target completion between 05:00 AM and 07:00 AM) using updated market data to establish current portfolio risk baselines.
●	Pre-Deal Check Functionality: Traders must be able to execute a pre-deal check from the Trade Pad.
●	Incremental Risk Calculation: The engine must evaluate the candidate deal against current portfolio risks and output isolated incremental CVA and FVA charges.
●	Broker Flow Generation: Incremental risk charges must attach automatically as broker flows payable to the PCVA desk. Opposite-direction trades that reduce overall portfolio risk must output negative values (risk releases).
5.2 End-of-Day Viewer (CVA Viewer) Workflow
●	Static Aggregate Calculations: Compute daily EOD XVA provisions using a fixed snapshot of the Sydney Closing CSA market dataset.
●	Immutability: EOD viewer figures must remain static once calculated to preserve official end-of-day audit trails.
●	Multi-View Dashboards: Results must display through structured dashboard views, enabling users to drill down from parent-level counterparties to trade-level attributions and risk factor sensitivities.
5.3 Technical Calculation Methodology & Input Rules
●	Monte Carlo Simulation: Exposure calculation must use Monte Carlo simulations diffusing market risk factors across 8,190 scenario paths over a 40-year horizon.
●	Discretized Time Bucketing: Simulations must evaluate exposures across ~200 discrete future maturity buckets (compact daily steps for days 1–14, transitioning to weekly, monthly, quarterly, and yearly intervals).
●	Positive Exposure Grid: CVA calculations must evaluate strictly positive MTM values ($Max(MTM, 0)$).
●	Credit Parameters: Probability of Default (PD) must draw from specific counterparty credit curves or generic sector/region/rating curves. Loss Given Default (LGD) must default to 40% (60% recovery rate).
●	Rate & FX Diffusion Process:
○	Rate processes across currencies must use the Single-Factor Hull-White (1F) model.
○	All FX risk factor diffusions must be processed against USD as the primary diffusion and funding currency.
○	Output reporting currency must be set to Australian Dollars (AUD).
●	Segregated Variation Margin (VM) Special Handling: For counterparties holding Segregated VM CSAs, the engine must force the Funding Benefit Adjustment (FBA) parameter to zero due to legal collateral re-hypothecation restrictions.
